  "live_records": {
    "q-319092": {
      "dom_id": "step-q319092",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "For the matrix\n$Y=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{13}$ of the entry ${y}_{13}.$\n\n${M}_{13}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The minor of ${y}_{13}=2$ (first row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & -2 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${y}_{13}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{13} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-2-0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
