    "q-319109": {
      "dom_id": "step-q319109",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "For the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the entry ${p}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The minor of ${p}_{12}=-2$ (first row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -2 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 6 & ∗ & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${p}_{12}=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =0-24 \\\\  & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
