      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is the minor of ${u}_{21}$ in the matrix\n$U=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & j & k-2j \\\\ kj & j & k \\\\ 7 & -k & j\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we remove the second row and the first column: \n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & j & k-2j \\\\ kj & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & -k & j\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}j & k-2j \\\\ -k & j\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}j & k-2j \\\\ -k & j\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =j\\cdot j-(-k)\\cdot (k-2j) \\\\  & ={j}^{2}+k(k-2j) \\\\  & ={j}^{2}+{k}^{2}-k2j \\\\  & ={j}^{2}-2jk+{k}^{2} \\\\  & =(j-k)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
