    "q-69760": {
      "dom_id": "step-q69760",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "What is the minor of ${t}_{33}$ in the matrix\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}y-x & x & {y}^{2} \\\\ -x & y+x & 1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & {y}^{2} & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}y-x & x & ∗ \\\\ -x & y+x & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}y-x & x \\\\ -x & y+x\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}y-x & x \\\\ -x & y+x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(y-x)\\cdot (y+x)-x\\cdot (-x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}^{2}}+\\cancel{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
