    "q-18240": {
      "dom_id": "step-q18240",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Given that the minor of ${d}_{31}$ is $43$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 9 & 11 & x \\\\ 7 & -5 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & -5 \\\\ ∗ & 11 & x \\\\ 7 & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${d}_{31}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot x-11\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =x+55.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${d}_{31}$ is $43$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+55 & =43 \\\\ x & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-12.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-18240-a",
